<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n83992" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πλούτων</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ωνος</span>,
			ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>Pluto,</i> god of the nether world, first in Trag., as
				<i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				806
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Ant.</u>
				1200
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Alc.</u>
				360
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>HF</u>
				808
			</span></i> (lyr.): acc. to Plato (from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλοῦτος</span>) the <i>wealth-giver,</i> a name of Hades,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅτι ἐκ τῆς γῆς ἀνίεται [ὁ
			πλοῦτος</span>], <i><span class="en">
				<u>Cra.</u>
				403a
			</span></i>, cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλουτοδότης;</span>
			identified with <i>Plutus,</i> and considered as the god of
			riches, cf. <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				273
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Pl.</u>
				727
			</span></i>:—hence <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πλουτώνιος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to
			Pluto;</i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
</div>